<http://data.silknow.org/object/f71bffcb-4afe-33db-b0ee-a1014976f8fa/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Scarf of cotton with 1.5 inch wide stripes formed by many narrow stripes of silk. Seven cotton warp threads and six silk warp threads interwoven with the silk mainly to the surface, all in a very pale lime green. Between the stripes are brocaded silk flower heads in profile with pink petals, green calyx and black stems, scattered in an unconnected zig zag. There is a narrow selvedge at each side in the pale line green silk.\n\nThe flower heads are brocaded in fancy twill. Narrow stripes of 7 cotton warp threads and 6 silk warp threads woven in basket or brick formation."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f71bffcb-4afe-33db-b0ee-a1014976f8fa> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/f71bffcb-4afe-33db-b0ee-a1014976f8fa>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Scarf of cotton with 1.5 inch wide stripes formed by many narrow stripes of silk. Seven cotton warp threads and six silk warp threads interwoven with the silk mainly to the surface, all in a very pale lime green. Between the stripes are brocaded silk flower heads in profile with pink petals, green calyx and black stems, scattered in an unconnected zig zag. There is a narrow selvedge at each side in the pale line green silk.\n\nThe flower heads are brocaded in fancy twill. Narrow stripes of 7 cotton warp threads and 6 silk warp threads woven in basket or brick formation."@en , "Scarf of brocaded cotton and silk, England, 1800-1820."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/52fc442b-b510-363d-80ab-ad7df94be724> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Scarf of brocaded cotton and silk, England, 1800-1820."@en , "Scarf of cotton with 1.5 inch wide stripes formed by many narrow stripes of silk. Seven cotton warp threads and six silk warp threads interwoven with the silk mainly to the surface, all in a very pale lime green. Between the stripes are brocaded silk flower heads in profile with pink petals, green calyx and black stems, scattered in an unconnected zig zag. There is a narrow selvedge at each side in the pale line green silk.\n\nThe flower heads are brocaded in fancy twill. Narrow stripes of 7 cotton warp threads and 6 silk warp threads woven in basket or brick formation."@en ;
